<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
  <title>Concept C — Industrial Machine</title>
  <style>
    :root{--bg:#c9c5bb;--ink:#111314;--panel:#1a1d1e;--paper:#e6e1d6;--line:#696b68;--orange:#d75d2b;--muted:#555a5c;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink)}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:repeating-linear-gradient(90deg,rgba(0,0,0,.025) 0 1px,transparent 1px 120px),var(--bg)}a{color:inherit}.rail{position:fixed;left:0;top:0;bottom:0;width:12px;background:var(--orange);z-index:10}.wrap{width:min(1220px,calc(100% - 4rem));margin:auto}.header{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr auto auto;gap:2rem;align-items:center;padding:1.2rem 0;border-bottom:3px solid var(--ink);font:800 .7rem/1 ui-monospace,monospace;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase}.header a{text-decoration:none;border-bottom:1px solid}.hero{display:grid;grid-template-columns:.92fr 1.08fr;gap:3rem;padding:5rem 0 3rem}.label{font:800 .68rem/1 ui-monospace,monospace;letter-spacing:.13em;text-transform:uppercase}.hero h1{font-size:clamp(4rem,7.7vw,8rem);line-height:.83;letter-spacing:-.075em;margin:.7rem 0 1.5rem;max-width:7.5ch}.hero .lead{font-size:1.22rem;line-height:1.55;max-width:37rem}.machine{background:var(--panel);color:#f4f1ea;padding:1.2rem;border-left:12px solid var(--orange);align-self:stretch}.machine-top{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;border-bottom:1px solid #686d6f;padding-bottom:.8rem;font:800 .66rem/1 ui-monospace,monospace;letter-spacing:.1em}.machine svg{width:100%;display:block}.machine .caption{border-top:1px solid #686d6f;padding-top:.8rem;color:#afb7b9;font:600 .68rem/1.5 ui-monospace,monospace}.bar{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(5,1fr);border:2px solid var(--ink);margin-bottom:4rem}.bar div{padding:1rem;border-right:1px solid var(--ink)}.bar div:last-child{border:0}.bar span{display:block;font:800 .62rem/1 ui-monospace,monospace;letter-spacing:.11em;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:.7rem}.bar strong{font-size:.98rem}.section{padding:4rem 0;border-top:2px solid var(--ink);display:grid;grid-template-columns:14rem 1fr;gap:3rem}.section>.label{color:#25292a}.section h2{font-size:clamp(2.6rem,5vw,5rem);line-height:.9;letter-spacing:-.055em;margin:0 0 1.2rem;max-width:12ch}.section p{font-size:1.08rem;line-height:1.65;max-width:47rem}.systems{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:1rem;margin-top:2rem}.system{background:var(--paper);border:1px solid #72736f;padding:1.2rem;min-height:15rem;position:relative}.system:before{content:"";position:absolute;left:0;top:0;width:5rem;height:6px;background:var(--orange)}.system span{font:800 .64rem/1 ui-monospace,monospace;letter-spacing:.12em}.system h3{font-size:1.45rem;margin:2.2rem 0 .8rem}.system p{font-size:.95rem;color:#4f5354}.load{margin-top:3rem;background:#151718;color:#f1eee7;padding:1.5rem;border-left:12px solid var(--orange)}.load-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:8rem 1fr;gap:1rem;border-bottom:1px solid #505557;padding:.9rem 0}.load-grid:last-child{border-bottom:0}.load-grid b{font:800 .68rem/1.4 ui-monospace,monospace;color:#f08453}.load-grid span{font:600 .78rem/1.5 ui-monospace,monospace;color:#c0c7c9}.quote{padding:6rem 0;border-top:2px solid var(--ink)}.quote p{font-size:clamp(2.8rem,6vw,6.5rem);line-height:.9;letter-spacing:-.06em;margin:0;max-width:13ch}.footer{padding:2rem 0 4rem;border-top:1px solid var(--line);font:800 .66rem/1.5 ui-monospace,monospace;color:var(--muted)}@media(max-width:850px){.hero,.section{grid-template-columns:1fr}.bar{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.bar div{border-bottom:1px solid var(--ink)}.systems{grid-template-columns:1fr}}@media(max-width:520px){.wrap{width:calc(100% - 2rem)}.header{grid-template-columns:1fr}.bar{grid-template-columns:1fr}.rail{width:7px}}
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="rail"></div>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="header"><span>Skyhook Industries / Concept C</span><span>Industrial Machine</span><a href="/concepts/">← All directions</a></header>
    <main>
      <section class="hero">
        <div><p class="label">Orbital momentum-transfer infrastructure</p><h1>Build the machine that replaces part of the rocket.</h1><p class="lead">A Skyhook stays in orbit, takes a payload from a high-altitude vehicle, and does the next part of the acceleration with a reusable rotating structure instead of another expendable propulsion stage.</p></div>
        <div class="machine">
          <div class="machine-top"><span>TETHER ASSEMBLY / STUDY CUTAWAY</span><span>SECTIONAL LOAD PATH</span></div>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 680 470" role="img" aria-label="Industrial cutaway concept for a redundant sectional tether">
            <rect x="70" y="88" width="540" height="255" rx="8" fill="#222627" stroke="#737a7d"/>
            <line x1="105" y1="145" x2="575" y2="145" stroke="#e9eceb" stroke-width="7"/>
            <line x1="105" y1="190" x2="575" y2="190" stroke="#9ea8ac" stroke-width="5"/>
            <line x1="105" y1="235" x2="575" y2="235" stroke="#e9eceb" stroke-width="7"/>
            <line x1="105" y1="280" x2="575" y2="280" stroke="#9ea8ac" stroke-width="5"/>
            <g stroke="#d75d2b" stroke-width="5"><line x1="205" y1="108" x2="205" y2="323"/><line x1="340" y1="108" x2="340" y2="323"/><line x1="475" y1="108" x2="475" y2="323"/></g>
            <g fill="#f0eee8" font-family="monospace" font-size="12"><text x="98" y="130">PRIMARY A</text><text x="98" y="177">SECONDARY A</text><text x="98" y="222">PRIMARY B</text><text x="98" y="267">SECONDARY B</text><text x="185" y="373">SECTION BREAK</text><text x="316" y="394">ISOLATABLE BAY</text><text x="457" y="373">SECTION BREAK</text></g>
            <g stroke="#8b9396" stroke-dasharray="4 5"><line x1="205" y1="327" x2="205" y2="355"/><line x1="340" y1="327" x2="340" y2="377"/><line x1="475" y1="327" x2="475" y2="355"/></g>
          </svg>
          <p class="caption">CONCEPT ONLY / REDUNDANT LOAD PATHS / SECTIONAL ISOLATION / TAPER NOT SHOWN / MATERIAL SYSTEM UNRESOLVED</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="bar"><div><span>OBJECT</span><strong>Rotating orbital tether</strong></div><div><span>LENGTH CLASS</span><strong>Thousands of km</strong></div><div><span>STRUCTURE</span><strong>Tapered + redundant</strong></div><div><span>SERVICE MODEL</span><strong>Reusable infrastructure</strong></div><div><span>GROUND ANCHOR</span><strong>None</strong></div></div>

      <section class="section">
        <p class="label">The engineering program</p>
        <div><h2>Stop talking about “a tether” as though it were one rope.</h2><p>A transportation-scale Skyhook would be a distributed machine: structural members, conductors, capture hardware, power systems, guidance, inspection, fault isolation and orbital-control systems spread over an extraordinary distance.</p><p>The useful design question is not “what material is strong enough?” It is whether the complete structure can carry cyclic load, survive local damage, be inspected, isolate failed sections and keep operating long enough to justify putting it in orbit.</p>
          <div class="systems"><article class="system"><span>01 / LOAD PATH</span><h3>Redundant structure</h3><p>Multiple separated members carry the load so a single cut does not define the fate of the whole tether.</p></article><article class="system"><span>02 / SECTIONS</span><h3>Controlled boundaries</h3><p>Long spans are broken into defined structural and operational sections with known interfaces and failure behavior.</p></article><article class="system"><span>03 / CAPTURE END</span><h3>Serviceable hardware</h3><p>The part that meets a vehicle is treated as machinery: inspectable, replaceable and designed around repeated shock loading.</p></article><article class="system"><span>04 / RECOVERY</span><h3>Orbital control</h3><p>Every mission changes the system’s orbit. Reboost is not an accessory; it is part of the transportation cycle.</p></article></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <p class="label">Failure philosophy</p>
        <div><h2>Design for damage before designing for perfection.</h2><p>Micrometeoroids, debris, fatigue, thermal cycling and deployment errors are not edge cases for a structure this large. A credible Skyhook must assume that parts of it will eventually be damaged and decide in advance what the rest of the machine does next.</p>
          <div class="load"><div class="load-grid"><b>LOCAL CUT</b><span>REDISTRIBUTE LOAD / RETAIN CONTINUITY / FLAG SECTION FOR INSPECTION</span></div><div class="load-grid"><b>TRACKED OBJECT</b><span>PREDICT CONJUNCTION / MANEUVER WHEN PRACTICAL / PROTECT HIGH-RISK HARDWARE</span></div><div class="load-grid"><b>SECTION LOSS</b><span>ISOLATE / CONTROL POST-SEVER DYNAMICS / MINIMIZE DEBRIS AND RE-ENTRY RISK</span></div></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <p class="label">Design language</p><div><h2>What this direction says about Skyhook.</h2><p>This version treats the project as infrastructure rather than wonder. It is the strongest language for structural design, failure management, materials, maintenance and the eventual hardware program. It feels more like a bridge authority, heavy aerospace contractor or launch-range engineering group than a startup.</p><p>Used alone, it is probably too earthbound for the homepage. Used inside the final design, it can keep the cinematic sections honest.</p></div>
      </section>

      <section class="quote"><p>The point is not to build a spectacular object. The point is to build an object that can do the same job again.</p></section>
    </main>
    <footer class="footer">SKYHOOK INDUSTRIES / DESIGN STUDY / CONCEPT C / INDUSTRIAL MACHINE</footer>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
